  "title": "ftypes: Allow comparing unsigned and signed integers",
  "description": "Allow signed and unsigned integer ftypes to be compared. We\nalways currently call the compare function of the left hand side\ntype. If the right hand side fails to convert to the appropriate\ntype due to integer underflow, we know the LHS is greater. If\nthe RHS fails to convert due to overflow, we know the LHS is lesser.\n\nPing #18960\n\n(There are some other corner cases in that issue, plus we might want\nto warn/fail on comparisons to constants that are outside type limits\nand always true or always false.)",
